msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-performance.php:2191
msgid ""
"Without those two attributes the browser cannot reserve the space, so "
"everything below each image jumps down when it finally arrives. This is what "
"Core Web Vitals measures as layout shift, and it is the single most "
"irritating thing a page can do to a reader. Turn on content image "
"optimization below, and for images printed by the theme rather than by the "
"content, ask its author — or replace them with images from the media "
"library, which carry their size."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of images, 2: total images on the page.
#: includes/admin/trait-performance.php:2200
#, php-format
msgid "%1$d of the %2$d images on your home page load immediately"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-performance.php:2204
msgid ""
"Images the visitor has not scrolled to yet are competing for bandwidth with "
"the ones they can already see, so the visible part of the page finishes "
"later than it needs to. Content image optimization adds the deferral "
"automatically and leaves the first image eager, which is the one that should "
"load first."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of images, 2: total images on the page.
#: includes/admin/trait-performance.php:2213
#, php-format
msgid "%1$d of the %2$d images on your home page offer only one size"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-performance.php:2217
msgid ""
"With no list of alternative sizes, a phone downloads the same file a desktop "
"does — often several times larger than its screen can show. Images inserted "
"from the media library get that list from WordPress automatically; ones hard-"
"coded in a template or pasted as raw HTML do not."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of HTML elements.
#: includes/admin/trait-performance.php:2226
#, php-format
msgid "Your home page is built from %d HTML elements"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-performance.php:2229
msgid ""
"Past roughly 1,400 elements the browser spends real time on style and layout "
"for every change on the page, and past 2,500 it is the dominant cost — "
"whatever the server does. The usual cause is a page builder nesting rows "
"inside columns inside containers, or a very long archive. Showing fewer "
"items per page, or flattening the sections you build most often, does more "
"here than any server-side setting."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of elements carrying a style attribute.
#: includes/admin/trait-performance.php:2238
#, php-format
msgid "%d elements on your home page carry their own inline styles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-performance.php:2241
msgid ""
"A style attribute cannot be cached, minified or reused between pages: it is "
"re-sent in full with every request. At this volume a builder is writing a "
"stylesheet one element at a time. Check whether it offers a “load CSS as a "
"file” or “combine styles” option — that alone moves the weight into "
"something the browser can cache."
