#: includes/opcache-health.php:243
msgid "PHP OPcache is switched off"
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:244
msgid ""
"Without OPcache, PHP compiles every file of WordPress, your theme and every "
"plugin on every single request. Enabling it is the single largest server-"
"side improvement available, and it is a one-line change your host can make: "
"opcache.enable=1."
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:249
msgid "OPcache is being rebuilt constantly"
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:250
msgid ""
"The compiled-code cache has started over on several page loads in a row. On "
"this kind of server it lives inside the PHP worker processes, so when the "
"last one is closed for being idle it is thrown away and rebuilt from nothing "
"for the next visitor. More memory will not help. Ask your host to stop PHP "
"workers being recycled while idle — on LiteSpeed that is the external "
"application's “Max Idle Time” (set it to -1) and PHP_LSAPI_MAX_REQUESTS."
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:255
msgid "OPcache keeps running out of memory"
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:256
msgid ""
"OPcache has restarted itself because it filled up, which throws away every "
"compiled file and recompiles them from scratch. This is the one number that "
"says so directly, and the fix is exact: raise opcache.memory_consumption "
"(256M or more on a site with many plugins)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:261
msgid "OPcache has run out of file slots"
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:262
msgid ""
"It is not short of memory — it is short of places to put files, so the ones "
"that do not fit are recompiled on every request. Raise "
"opcache.max_accelerated_files above the number of PHP files on the site "
"(30000 or more is normal for WordPress with a page builder and a few dozen "
"plugins)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:267
msgid "OPcache's string buffer is full"
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:268
msgid ""
"Repeated strings are shared between compiled files to save memory, and that "
"buffer is full, so the saving stops. Raise opcache.interned_strings_buffer "
"(16 to 32 MB)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:273
msgid "OPcache memory is fragmenting"
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:274
msgid ""
"A large share of the cache is taken up by versions of files that have since "
"changed. This is normal right after an update and clears itself on the next "
"restart; if it stays high, files are being modified on every request — a "
"plugin writing PHP, or a cache directory inside the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:279
msgid "OPcache is recompiling more than it should"
msgstr ""

#: includes/opcache-health.php:280
msgid ""
"Nothing is obviously misconfigured — the cache is not full, has not "
"restarted and has been running long enough to judge — so this is worth "
"watching rather than acting on immediately. If it stays low, the usual cause "
"is files changing on disk during normal traffic."
msgstr ""

