"CSS and JavaScript minification (opt-in, off by default): under Speed › Page "
"& browser › Minification WPOptimizing can serve minified copies of your own "
"local CSS and JS, stripping comments and whitespace so they download faster. "
"It is deliberately conservative: files that are already minified, hosted on "
"another domain, or listed in your exclusions are left untouched; the "
"minified copies live in wp-content/uploads/wpopt-assets/ and are rebuilt "
"automatically when the source changes or a cache is flushed. A test mode "
"lets administrators preview the result before exposing it to visitors, and "
"it refuses to run alongside another asset optimizer (Autoptimize, WP Rocket, "
"Perfmatters, LiteSpeed) to avoid double-processing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-docs.php:169
msgid ""
"Optional speed features for the public site, configured in Speed › Page & "
"browser: speculative loading (prefetch/prerender the next page), content "
"image loading optimization, resource hints and a Server-Timing diagnostic "
"header. All opt-in and reversible; none cache full HTML pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-docs.php:170
msgid ""
"Settings: Max dimensions set separate width and height limits (0 on an axis "
"disables it). Scale down oversized uploads applies them to new uploads "
"through WordPress' native handling, which keeps the full-size original."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-docs.php:171
msgid ""
"Removes database clutter: post revisions, auto-drafts, trashed posts, spam "
"comments, and expired transients. Runs from a single button. A detailed log "
"is saved after every run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-docs.php:172
msgid ""
"Every batch the cleanup deletes is backed up first, into one Backups entry "
"per run. If that backup cannot be written, the run stops with the status "
"“Stopped: backup failed” and deletes nothing more. Table optimization "
"changes no data and needs no backup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-docs.php:173
msgid ""
"Scans your uploads for files with no database attachment record, orphaned "
"thumbnail sizes and potentially unused attachments, and counts the exact-"
"content duplicates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-docs.php:174
msgid ""
"Every change WPOptimizing makes to your data is backed up first: deletions "
"(orphans, empty rows, media and the general cleanup) and changes (autoload "
"flags, scheduled tasks, .htaccess and wp-config.php edits). Backups are "
"grouped by operation so you can find and restore exactly what a specific "
"action changed. Manual backups can also be created at any time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-media.php:825
msgid ""
"Uploads larger than this (width × height) are scaled down when they are "
"uploaded; the full-size original is kept. 0 on an axis disables it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-media.php:835
msgid ""
"Scale down oversized uploads to the max dimensions — the full-size original "
"is preserved"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-media.php:1276
msgid ""
"The media library audit (stranded and competing files, leftover sizes, "
"downloadable dumps and logs, and the uploads protection) is not included in "
"this plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-media.php:1278
msgid "The media library audit is part of Pro and needs an active license."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-media.php:1495
msgid ""
"Listing duplicate images and merging them (one copy kept, its references "
"reassigned) is not included in this plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-performance.php:68
msgid ""
"How the page reaches the visitor: speculative loading, image loading, "
"resource hints and a Server-Timing diagnostic. All optional and reversible; "
"none of them cache whole pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-settings.php:692
msgid ""
"Scheduled cleanup (hourly to monthly, with a frequency per task) and "
"automatic cleanup when the database grows are not included in this plugin. "
"Run the cleanup from General cleanup whenever you need it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-settings.php:694
msgid ""
"Scheduled cleanup and automatic cleanup when the database grows are part of "
"Pro and need an active license. Your schedule is kept and comes back with "
"the license."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-settings.php:920
msgid ""
"Webhooks are part of Pro and need an active license. The endpoint you saved "
"is kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-settings.php:1119
msgid ""
"Preloading key resources, lazy YouTube embeds, self-hosted Google Fonts and "
"CDN rewriting are not included in this plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-settings.php:1121
msgid ""
"Preloading key resources, lazy YouTube embeds, self-hosted Google Fonts and "
"CDN rewriting are part of Pro and need an active license."
