msgid "The WPOptimizing API needs an active Pro license."
msgstr ""

#: includes/cli.php:275
msgid "The WPOptimizing commands need an active Pro license."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-docs.php:167
msgid ""
"Import / export: download the whole configuration as a JSON file and restore "
"it here or on another site — handy to replicate your setup across a fleet. "
"The export covers the settings for cleanup, cache, media and images, backups "
"and attribution. For safety it never includes keys, passwords, the data-"
"sharing consent, branding or measured runtime state (scan results, "
"baselines, cached sizes), so importing onto another site only carries "
"configuration. On import, existing settings are overwritten and any "
"unrecognized keys are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-docs.php:176
msgid ""
"Every media deletion is backed up first, so it is reversible: WPOptimizing "
"copies each file before removing anything. If you ever need to undo a "
"deletion, the Media tab shows how many file backups are available and links "
"straight to the Backups tab, where you restore a whole operation in one "
"click. Nothing is deleted that was not fully backed up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-docs.php:177
msgid ""
"Image optimization (front-end WebP/AVIF serving, scaling down oversized "
"uploads and the analysis of the library) has its own sub-section, documented "
"separately under Image optimization."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-docs.php:178
msgid ""
"Media has six entries: Orphans (with a filter for orphan files, orphan "
"thumbnails and other files), Duplicate sets, Unused attachments, Image "
"optimization (Summary and Heaviest images), Trash and Library audit. Merging "
"duplicates and the library audit are not included in this plugin: their "
"entries only say so."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-media.php:1101
msgid ""
"Finds files in /uploads with no record in the database, orphaned thumbnails "
"and unused attachments, and counts the duplicate media. Media deletions are "
"backed up first and can be restored from the Backups tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-settings.php:348
msgid ""
"Configure cleanup options and backups. Quick profiles below apply a "
"recommended configuration with one click."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-settings.php:809
msgid ""
"Speculative loading, image loading, resource hints and Server-Timing are now "
"under Speed › Page & browser, next to minify."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/trait-settings.php:1538
msgid ""
"Save this site’s configuration to a JSON file and restore it here or on "
"another site — handy to replicate your setup across sites. It includes the "
"settings for cleanup, cache, media and images, backups and attribution. "
"Keys, passwords, data-sharing consent and measured runtime state (scan "
"results, baselines, cached sizes) are never included."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/screen.php:1402
msgid ""
"All the WPO your WordPress needs in a single plugin, with the only cleanup "
"that knows who owns each leftover before you delete anything."
msgstr ""

